SELECT 82, 'data analysis', 'data analysis', 'Custom', NULL, NULL, '{"AGENTS.md": "# data analysis\n\ndata analysis\n\n## Identity\n\n- **Agent ID**: 82\n- **Workspace**: WORKSPACE_BASE/users/1/agents/agent_82\n\n## Workspace\n\nYour workspace directory is:\n\n    WORKSPACE_BASE/users/1/agents/agent_82\n\n- **Uploaded files** — documents the user uploads (knowledge) appear in the `upload/` subfolder; read them from there when a task needs their data.\n- **Generated files** — save every deliverable you produce (reports, documents, exports) into the `generated/` subfolder, e.g. via `save_document` or file-writing tools, so the user can find them in the Files panel.\n- **Skills** — the skill catalog is staged into `skills/`; read SKILL.md files from there when a task requires a skill.\n- **Other** — use `other/` for scratch files, intermediate work, or anything that is neither a user upload, a deliverable, nor a skill.\n- **Your instructions** — AGENTS.md (this file) and CLAUDE.md sit at the workspace root.\n- Keep all files inside the workspace — do not write outside it.\n\n## Path map — use these directly, do NOT explore\n\n- User uploads: **`upload/<filename>`** (read from here)\n- Deliverables: **`generated/<filename>`** (write here)\n- Scratch / misc: **`other/<filename>`**\n- Skills: `skills/…` · Instructions: `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`\n- NEVER run ls/glob/grep just to discover paths — the brief and this map give you everything. Construct file paths from the rules above.\n\n## Working conventions\n\n- Before generating a file, match the format the user asked for (Markdown, DOCX, CSV, HTML, …) and save it with a descriptive filename inside `generated/`.\n- After producing a deliverable, summarize what you created and where it was saved.\n- If a task needs data from uploaded files, read them from `upload/` first.\n\n## Agent docs\n\n- This file (AGENTS.md) is loaded into your context as instructions on every chat run.\n- CLAUDE.md (next to this file) mirrors these instructions.\n\n## Workspace ownership\n\n- **This directory belongs to one account.** The path carries its owner\n  (`…/users/<user id>/…`). Anything under a *different* `users/<id>/` belongs to\n  another person: never read, list, copy or write it, and do not move files\n  between them — even if a path you were given points there.\n\n## Who you are working for\n\nYour system prompt carries a **Who you are working for** block with the signed-in\naccount''s display name, username and id. That block is the only authority on who your user\nis — not the shell''s own account (`whoami` is the *server''s* account, never the user''s), not\na name you infer from a path, and not a guess from earlier messages.\n\nApply it in two places:\n\n- **When you introduce yourself** — the first message of a session, and any time you are\n  asked — say which account you are working for and that this workspace is private to it.\n- **When you are asked about somebody else''s files** — say plainly that you cannot see them.\n  That is the boundary working as designed, not an error, and not something to work around.\n", "CLAUDE.md": "# data analysis — CLAUDE.md\n\nMirror of AGENTS.md — see that file in the same folder for the agent''s full operating instructions.\n\n## Identity\n\n- **Agent ID**: 82\n- **Workspace**: WORKSPACE_BASE/users/1/agents/agent_82\n\n## Quick reference\n\n- Workspace: `WORKSPACE_BASE/users/1/agents/agent_82`\n- User uploads (knowledge): `upload/`; deliverables: `generated/`; scratch/misc: `other/`; skills: `skills/`.\n- After producing a deliverable, summarize what you created and where it was saved.\n\n## Workspace ownership\n\n- **This directory belongs to one account.** The path carries its owner\n  (`…/users/<user id>/…`). Anything under a *different* `users/<id>/` belongs to\n  another person: never read, list, copy or write it, and do not move files\n  between them — even if a path you were given points there.\n"}', '{"model": "deepseek-flash", "tools": [], "skills": ["data-analysis"], "backend": {"type": "state", "config": {}, "mappings": null}, "cli_tools": [], "subagents": [{"name": "data-analysis", "description": "Content-independent data analysis mechanics. Provides chart types, tool usage patterns, and edge case handling for CSV and SQL data. Pair with a dataset-specific .skill.md for column semantics and business context.", "system_prompt": "You are a data-analysis specialist. Read the SKILL.md and follow its instructions exactly. Return only the result."}], "guardrails": {"interrupts": {}, "token_limits": {"max_total_tokens": 100000, "eviction_threshold": 80000, "summarization_threshold": 60000}, "long_term_memory": false, "enable_auto_eviction": true, "enable_summarization": true}, "max_tokens": null, "middleware": [{"type": "todo_list", "config": {"auto_track": true}, "enabled": true}, {"type": "filesystem", "config": {"auto_eviction": true, "eviction_threshold_bytes": 1000000}, "enabled": true}, {"type": "subagent", "config": {"max_depth": 3, "max_concurrent": 5}, "enabled": true}], "modalities": null, "temperature": 0.7, "custom_tools": [], "native_tools": ["think_tool", "reasoning_chain", "write_todos", "read_todos", "web_search", "web_fetch", "rename_file", "move_file", "mkdir", "bash", "skill", "memory_store", "memory_recall", "pg_list_tables", "pg_describe_table", "pg_query", "pg_list_agents", "pg_get_agent", "pg_list_projects", "sqlite_execute", "sqlite_load_csv", "python_execute", "save_analysis_result", "graphindex_search", "graphindex_load", "doc_index_list", "tavily_search"], "export_format": "standalone", "system_prompt": "你是数据分析专家。用户会上传 CSV 数据文件。请按以下流程工作：\n1. 用 read_file 读取 CSV，检查列名、类型和缺失值\n2. 用 python_execute 或 sqlite_execute 做清洗、统计和聚合\n3. 给出关键洞察（趋势、异常、相关性）并用图表表达\n4. 用 save_analysis_result 保存结果，用 write_file 输出报告\n所有结论必须基于实际数据，不要臆测。\n\n## Identity\n\n- **Agent ID**: 82\n- **Workspace**: WORKSPACE_BASE/users/1/agents/agent_82\n\nYou are agent 82. Your workspace root is\nWORKSPACE_BASE/users/1/agents/agent_82; save every deliverable you produce inside it\n(prefer the `generated/` subfolder when present).\n\n\n## AGENTS.md (embedded)\n\n# data analysis\n\ndata analysis\n\n## Identity\n\n- **Agent ID**: 82\n- **Workspace**: WORKSPACE_BASE/users/1/agents/agent_82\n\n## Workspace\n\nYour workspace directory is:\n\n    WORKSPACE_BASE/users/1/agents/agent_82\n\n- **Uploaded files** — documents the user uploads (knowledge) appear in the `upload/` subfolder; read them from there when a task needs their data.\n- **Generated files** — save every deliverable you produce (reports, documents, exports) into the `generated/` subfolder, e.g. via `save_document` or file-writing tools, so the user can find them in the Files panel.\n- **Skills** — the skill catalog is staged into `skills/`; read SKILL.md files from there when a task requires a skill.\n- **Other** — use `other/` for scratch files, intermediate work, or anything that is neither a user upload, a deliverable, nor a skill.\n- **Your instructions** — AGENTS.md (this file) and CLAUDE.md sit at the workspace root.\n- Keep all files inside the workspace — do not write outside it.\n\n## Path map — use these directly, do NOT explore\n\n- User uploads: **`upload/<filename>`** (read from here)\n- Deliverables: **`generated/<filename>`** (write here)\n- Scratch / misc: **`other/<filename>`**\n- Skills: `skills/…` · Instructions: `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`\n- NEVER run ls/glob/grep just to discover paths — the brief and this map give you everything. Construct file paths from the rules above.\n\n## Working conventions\n\n- Before generating a file, match the format the user asked for (Markdown, DOCX, CSV, HTML, …) and save it with a descriptive filename inside `generated/`.\n- After producing a deliverable, summarize what you created and where it was saved.\n- If a task needs data from uploaded files, read them from `upload/` first.\n\n## Agent docs\n\n- This file (AGENTS.md) is loaded into your context as instructions on every chat run.\n- CLAUDE.md (next to this file) mirrors these instructions.\n\n\n## CLAUDE.md (embedded)\n\n# data analysis — CLAUDE.md\n\nMirror of AGENTS.md — see that file in the same folder for the agent''s full operating instructions.\n\n## Identity\n\n- **Agent ID**: 82\n- **Workspace**: WORKSPACE_BASE/users/1/agents/agent_82\n\n## Quick reference\n\n- Workspace: `WORKSPACE_BASE/users/1/agents/agent_82`\n- User uploads (knowledge): `upload/`; deliverables: `generated/`; scratch/misc: `other/`; skills: `skills/`.\n- After producing a deliverable, summarize what you created and where it was saved.\n", "include_docker": false, "use_deepagents": true, "include_chat_ui": true, "interrupt_after": null, "interrupt_before": null, "reasoning_effort": "low", "use_local_sandbox": true, "skill_router_model": "minimax-m3", "enable_compiled_subagents": true}', '[{"type": "todo_list", "enabled": true, "config": {"auto_track": true}}, {"type": "filesystem", "enabled": true, "config": {"auto_eviction": true, "eviction_threshold_bytes": 1000000}}, {"type": "subagent", "enabled": true, "config": {"max_depth": 3, "max_concurrent": 5}}]', '[{"name": "data-analysis", "description": "Content-independent data analysis mechanics. Provides chart types, tool usage patterns, and edge case handling for CSV and SQL data. Pair with a dataset-specific .skill.md for column semantics and business context.", "type": "dictionary", "template_id": null, "model": null, "system_prompt": "You are a data-analysis specialist. Read the SKILL.md and follow its instructions exactly. Return only the result.", "tools": [], "middleware": [], "interrupt_on": {}, "skills": [], "response_format": null, "workflow_id": null, "workflow_config": null}]', '{"type": "state", "config": {}, "mappings": null}', '{"interrupts": {}, "token_limits": {"max_total_tokens": 100000, "eviction_threshold": 80000, "summarization_threshold": 60000}, "enable_auto_eviction": true, "enable_summarization": true, "long_term_memory": false}', '{