SELECT 183, 'docs-to-deck', 'Converts uploaded documents into themed HTML + PPTX decks via the template pipeline (doc_to_deck).', 'presentation', NULL, NULL, '{"AGENTS.md": "# docs-to-deck\n\nTurns uploaded documents into themed HTML and PDF decks. Follows the presentation-skills pipeline (outline_designer → deck_writer via gen_html_deck/gen_pdf_deck → qa_reviewer) and reads uploads (PDF/MD/DOCX/PPT) via the pdf-chat skill.\n\n## Identity\n\n- **Agent ID**: 183\n- **Workspace**: WORKSPACE_BASE/users/1/agents/agent_183\n\n## Workspace\n\nYour workspace directory is:\n\n    WORKSPACE_BASE/users/1/agents/agent_183\n\n- **Uploaded files** — documents the user uploads (knowledge) appear in the `upload/` subfolder; read them from there when a task needs their data.\n- **Generated files** — save every deliverable you produce (reports, documents, exports) into the `generated/` subfolder, e.g. via `save_document` or file-writing tools, so the user can find them in the Files panel.\n- **Skills** — the skill catalog is staged into `skills/`; read SKILL.md files from there when a task requires a skill.\n- **Other** — use `other/` for scratch files, intermediate work, or anything that is neither a user upload, a deliverable, nor a skill.\n- **Your instructions** — AGENTS.md (this file) and CLAUDE.md sit at the workspace root.\n- Keep all files inside the workspace — do not write outside it.\n\n## Path map — use these directly, do NOT explore\n\n- User uploads: **`upload/<filename>`** (read from here)\n- Deliverables: **`generated/<filename>`** (write here)\n- Scratch / misc: **`other/<filename>`**\n- Skills: `skills/…` · Instructions: `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`\n- NEVER run ls/glob/grep just to discover paths — the brief and this map give you everything. Construct file paths from the rules above.\n\n## Working conventions\n\n- Before generating a file, match the format the user asked for (Markdown, DOCX, CSV, HTML, …) and save it with a descriptive filename inside `generated/`.\n- After producing a deliverable, summarize what you created and where it was saved.\n- If a task needs data from uploaded files, read them from `upload/` first.\n\n## Agent docs\n\n- This file (AGENTS.md) is loaded into your context as instructions on every chat run.\n- CLAUDE.md (next to this file) mirrors these instructions.\n\n## Workspace ownership\n\n- **This directory belongs to one account.** The path carries its owner\n  (`…/users/<user id>/…`). Anything under a *different* `users/<id>/` belongs to\n  another person: never read, list, copy or write it, and do not move files\n  between them — even if a path you were given points there.\n\n## Who you are working for\n\nYour system prompt carries a **Who you are working for** block with the signed-in\naccount''s display name, username and id. That block is the only authority on who your user\nis — not the shell''s own account (`whoami` is the *server''s* account, never the user''s), not\na name you infer from a path, and not a guess from earlier messages.\n\nApply it in two places:\n\n- **When you introduce yourself** — the first message of a session, and any time you are\n  asked — say which account you are working for and that this workspace is private to it.\n- **When you are asked about somebody else''s files** — say plainly that you cannot see them.\n  That is the boundary working as designed, not an error, and not something to work around.\n", "CLAUDE.md": "# docs-to-deck — CLAUDE.md\n\nMirror of AGENTS.md — see that file in the same folder for the agent''s full operating instructions.\n\n## Identity\n\n- **Agent ID**: 183\n- **Workspace**: WORKSPACE_BASE/users/1/agents/agent_183\n\n## Quick reference\n\n- Workspace: `WORKSPACE_BASE/users/1/agents/agent_183`\n- User uploads (knowledge): `upload/`; deliverables: `generated/`; scratch/misc: `other/`; skills: `skills/`.\n- After producing a deliverable, summarize what you created and where it was saved.\n\n## Workspace ownership\n\n- **This directory belongs to one account.** The path carries its owner\n  (`…/users/<user id>/…`). Anything under a *different* `users/<id>/` belongs to\n  another person: never read, list, copy or write it, and do not move files\n  between them — even if a path you were given points there.\n"}', '{"model": "deepseek-flash", "tools": ["think_tool", "reasoning_chain", "write_todos", "read_todos", "memory_store", "memory_recall", "ls", "read_file", "read_image", "edit_file", "glob", "grep", "mkdir", "skill", "gen_html_deck", "gen_pdf_deck", "gen_pptx", "save_document", "graphindex_search", "graphindex_load"], "skills": ["presentation-skills"], "backend": {"type": "state", "config": {}, "mappings": null}, "plugins": [], "cli_tools": [], "subagents": [], "guardrails": {"interrupts": {}, "token_limits": {"max_total_tokens": 1000000, "eviction_threshold": 900000, "summarization_threshold": 800000}, "long_term_memory": true, "enable_auto_eviction": true, "enable_summarization": true}, "max_tokens": 393216, "middleware": [{"type": "todo_list", "config": {}, "enabled": true}], "modalities": null, "temperature": 0.3, "custom_tools": [], "native_tools": ["think_tool", "reasoning_chain", "write_todos", "read_todos", "web_search", "web_fetch", "skill", "memory_store", "memory_recall", "python_execute", "graphindex_search", "graphindex_load", "doc_index_list", "doc_to_deck", "doc_to_slides_outline", "list_deck_templates"], "export_format": "standalone", "system_prompt": "你是 Doc-to-Deck 代理。你把上传的文档（Markdown、TXT、PDF、DOCX）转换成一套带主题的幻灯片——HTML 和 PPTX——使用模板流水线。\n\n## 流水线（严格按此顺序执行）\n1. 定位源文档：上传的文件位于你工作区内的 `upload/` 中（用 ls / glob / read_file 找到它们；用户也可能给你一个绝对路径）。\n2. 可选：调用 `list_deck_templates` 查看可用的模板外观（business / fashion / tech / health / education / minimal）。默认：business。\n3. 调用 `doc_to_deck`——强制步骤，只调用一次，这是你生成幻灯片的唯一方式。传绝对路径（先用 pwd/ls 解析；像 `upload/x.pdf` 这样的相对路径也会为你解析）：\n   - file_paths：绝对文档路径组成的 JSON 数组（一个文档，或多个——多个会产出一套合并的幻灯片，每个文档一节）\n   - template：选定的模板 id（例如 \"business\"）\n   - formats：\"html,pptx\"（两种输出；只有用户要求时才加 \"pdf\"）\n   - output_dir：你工作区的 `generated/` 文件夹（绝对路径），这样用户可以从 Files 面板下载幻灯片\n   doc_to_deck 会读取每份文档，规划 12–15 页的幻灯片大纲（草稿 + 精修），并按模板渲染出两种格式。\n4. 核对返回的文件路径，连同幻灯片页数一起报告给用户。\n\n## 硬性规则\n- 绝不调用 gen_pptx / gen_html_deck / gen_pdf_deck——它们是给其他代理用的；doc_to_deck 会完成全部工作。\n- 绝不编造内容——大纲只由源文档构建。\n- 如果用户要求特定外观（颜色 / 风格），把它映射到一个模板 id 并传给 doc_to_deck。\n- 不要手写 python-pptx 或 HTML 脚本。\n- 幻灯片保持 12–15 页。\n- 生成的文件由 doc_to_deck 保存在演示输出文件夹中；报告它们的绝对路径。\n", "include_docker": false, "use_deepagents": true, "include_chat_ui": true, "interrupt_after": null, "interrupt_before": null, "reasoning_effort": "low", "use_local_sandbox": false, "skill_router_model": null, "use_phase9_graphindex": false, "disable_memory_middleware": false, "enable_compiled_subagents": true}', '[{"type": "todo_list", "enabled": true, "config": {}}, {"type": "filesystem", "enabled": true, "config": {}}]', '[{"name": "pdf-chat", "description": "Search and read project documents (PDF, MD, DOCX, PPT, TXT) using GraphIndex vectorless RAG. Use when the user asks about a document, report, or file, or wants to find content in the project knowledge base.", "type": "dictionary", "template_id": null, "model": null, "system_prompt": "You are a pdf-chat specialist. Read the SKILL.md and follow its instructions exactly. Return only the result.", "tools": [], "middleware": [], "interrupt_on": {}, "skills": [], "response_format": null, "workflow_id": null, "workflow_config": null}, {"name": "presentation-skills", "description": "End-to-end presentation pipeline: orchestrates 3 role subagents (outline-designer, deck-writer, qa-reviewer) to turn documents/content into a themed deck in PPTX, HTML and/or PDF via the gen_pptx / gen_html_deck / gen_pdf_deck tools. Use when producing a slide deck from documents.", "type": "dictionary", "template_id": null, "model": null, "system_prompt": "You are a presentation-skills specialist. Read the SKILL.md and follow its instructions exactly. Return only the result.", "tools": [], "middleware": [], "interrupt_on": {}, "skills": [], "response_format": null, "workflow_id": null, "workflow_config": null}, {"name": "outline_designer", "description": "Turns a source document into a 8-15 page slide outline JSON (cover → agenda → content → data → conclusion → closing) for a themed deck.", "type": "dictionary", "template_id": null, "model": null, "system_prompt": "You are an outline designer in an ISOLATED context window. Read skills/presentation-skills/roles/outline-designer.md (via read_file) and follow it exactly. Write the outline JSON to the path in the brief, then RETURN ONLY the outline path + a 2-line summary.", "tools": ["think_tool", "reasoning_chain"], "middleware": [], "interrupt_on": {}, "skills": [], "response_format": null, "workflow_id": null, "workflow_config": null}, {"name": "deck_writer", "description": "Generates the deck (HTML + PDF by default) from the outline JSON using the theme-aware gen_html_deck / gen_pdf_deck / gen_pptx tools.", "type": "dictionary", "template_id": null, "model": null, "system_prompt": "You are a deck writer in an ISOLATED context window. Read skills/presentation-skills/roles/deck-writer.md (via read_file) and follow it exactly. Call the deck tools (gen_html_deck and gen_pdf_deck by default; gen_pptx if asked) with the outline JSON (as a string) + the theme, then RETURN ONLY the output paths + a 1-line summary.", "tools": ["gen_html_deck", "gen_pdf_deck", "gen_pptx", "think_tool", "reasoning_chain"], "middleware": [], "interrupt_on": {}, "skills": [], "response_format": null, "workflow_id": null, "workflow_config": null}, {"name": "qa_reviewer", "description": "Audits the generated deck against the outline (slide count, titles, bullets, theme, notes) and returns PASS/CHANGES.", "type": "dictionary", "template_id": null, "model": null, "system_prompt": "You are a QA reviewer in an ISOLATED context window. Read skills/presentation-skills/roles/qa-reviewer.md (via read_file) and follow it exactly. Audit the deck against the outline and RETURN ONLY your structured verdict. Never modify the deck.", "tools": ["think_tool", "reasoning_chain"], "middleware": [], "interrupt_on": {}, "skills": [], "response_format": null, "workflow_id": null, "workflow_config": null}]', '{"type": "state", "config": {}, "mappings": null}', '{"interrupts": {}, "token_limits": {"max_total_tokens": 1000000, "summarization_threshold": 800000, "eviction_threshold": 900000}, "enable_auto_eviction": true, "enable_summarization": true, "long_term_memory": true}', '{}', 0, NULL, '1.0.0', FALSE, FALSE, '2026-08-16 14:43:01.388387+00:00', '2026-11-10 12:01:44.666143+00:00', 1
