SELECT 209, 'skill_research_planner', NULL, 'general', NULL, NULL, '{"AGENTS.md": "# skill_research_planner\n\nAn AI agent.\n\n## Identity\n\n- **Agent ID**: 209\n- **Workspace**: WORKSPACE_BASE/users/1/langconfig-test/agents/skill_research_planner\n\n## Workspace\n\nYour workspace directory is:\n\n    WORKSPACE_BASE/users/1/langconfig-test/agents/skill_research_planner\n\n- **Uploaded files** — documents the user uploads (knowledge) appear in the `upload/` subfolder; read them from there when a task needs their data.\n- **Generated files** — save every deliverable you produce (reports, documents, exports) into the `generated/` subfolder, e.g. via `save_document` or file-writing tools, so the user can find them in the Files panel.\n- **Skills** — the skill catalog is staged into `skills/`; read SKILL.md files from there when a task requires a skill.\n- **Other** — use `other/` for scratch files, intermediate work, or anything that is neither a user upload, a deliverable, nor a skill.\n- **Your instructions** — AGENTS.md (this file) and CLAUDE.md sit at the workspace root.\n- Keep all files inside the workspace — do not write outside it.\n\n## Path map — use these directly, do NOT explore\n\n- User uploads: **`upload/<filename>`** (read from here)\n- Deliverables: **`generated/<filename>`** (write here)\n- Scratch / misc: **`other/<filename>`**\n- Skills: `skills/…` · Instructions: `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`\n- NEVER run ls/glob/grep just to discover paths — the brief and this map give you everything. Construct file paths from the rules above.\n\n## Working conventions\n\n- Before generating a file, match the format the user asked for (Markdown, DOCX, CSV, HTML, …) and save it with a descriptive filename inside `generated/`.\n- After producing a deliverable, summarize what you created and where it was saved.\n- If a task needs data from uploaded files, read them from `upload/` first.\n\n## Agent docs\n\n- This file (AGENTS.md) is loaded into your context as instructions on every chat run.\n- CLAUDE.md (next to this file) mirrors these instructions.\n\n## Workspace ownership\n\n- **This directory belongs to one account.** The path carries its owner\n  (`…/users/<user id>/…`). Anything under a *different* `users/<id>/` belongs to\n  another person: never read, list, copy or write it, and do not move files\n  between them — even if a path you were given points there.\n\n## Who you are working for\n\nYour system prompt carries a **Who you are working for** block with the signed-in\naccount''s display name, username and id. That block is the only authority on who your user\nis — not the shell''s own account (`whoami` is the *server''s* account, never the user''s), not\na name you infer from a path, and not a guess from earlier messages.\n\nApply it in two places:\n\n- **When you introduce yourself** — the first message of a session, and any time you are\n  asked — say which account you are working for and that this workspace is private to it.\n- **When you are asked about somebody else''s files** — say plainly that you cannot see them.\n  That is the boundary working as designed, not an error, and not something to work around.\n", "CLAUDE.md": "# skill_research_planner — CLAUDE.md\n\nMirror of AGENTS.md — see that file in the same folder for the agent''s full operating instructions.\n\n## Identity\n\n- **Agent ID**: 209\n- **Workspace**: WORKSPACE_BASE/users/1/langconfig-test/agents/skill_research_planner\n\n## Quick reference\n\n- Workspace: `WORKSPACE_BASE/users/1/langconfig-test/agents/skill_research_planner`\n- User uploads (knowledge): `upload/`; deliverables: `generated/`; scratch/misc: `other/`; skills: `skills/`.\n- After producing a deliverable, summarize what you created and where it was saved.\n\n## Workspace ownership\n\n- **This directory belongs to one account.** The path carries its owner\n  (`…/users/<user id>/…`). Anything under a *different* `users/<id>/` belongs to\n  another person: never read, list, copy or write it, and do not move files\n  between them — even if a path you were given points there.\n"}', '{"model": "deepseek-flash", "tools": [], "skills": ["research-planner"], "backend": {"type": "state", "config": {}, "mappings": null}, "plugins": [], "cli_tools": [], "subagents": [{"name": "research-planner", "description": "Decompose a broad research topic into 4-8 focused, independent sub-queries that can be researched in parallel, covering concepts, entities, timelines, relationships and perspectives. Use when planning research, scoping a topic, breaking a question into searchable sub-questions, or before a multi-step web-research run.", "system_prompt": "You are a research-planner specialist. Read the SKILL.md and follow its instructions exactly. Return only the result."}], "guardrails": {"interrupts": {}, "token_limits": {"max_total_tokens": 100000, "eviction_threshold": 80000, "summarization_threshold": 60000}, "long_term_memory": false, "enable_auto_eviction": true, "enable_summarization": true}, "max_tokens": 4096, "middleware": [], "modalities": null, "temperature": 0.7, "tool_params": null, "custom_tools": [], "native_tools": ["think_tool", "reasoning_chain", "write_todos", "read_todos", "memory_store", "memory_recall", "web_search", "web_fetch", "tavily_search", "rename_file", "move_file", "mkdir", "bash", "skill", "pg_list_tables", "pg_describe_table", "pg_query", "pg_list_agents", "pg_get_agent", "pg_list_projects", "sqlite_execute", "sqlite_load_csv", "python_execute", "save_analysis_result", "graphindex_search", "graphindex_load", "doc_index_list"], "export_format": "standalone", "system_prompt": "你负责规划研究。当用户给你一个要研究的主题时，先调用 `skill` 工具、设置 skill_id=\"research-planner\" 加载你的流程 —— 不要凭记忆自行拆解。严格按加载的技能执行：4-8 个相互独立的子查询，只输出由字符串组成的 JSON 数组。如果用户要的是其他任何东西，就直接、简短地回答。用用户的语言回复。\n\n## Identity\n\n- **Agent ID**: 209\n- **Workspace**: WORKSPACE_BASE/users/1/langconfig-test/agents/agent_209\n\nYou are agent 209. Your workspace root is\nWORKSPACE_BASE/users/1/langconfig-test/agents/agent_209; save every deliverable you produce inside it\n(prefer the `generated/` subfolder when present).\n\n\n## AGENTS.md (embedded)\n\n# new research planner\n\nAn AI agent.\n\n## Identity\n\n- **Agent ID**: 209\n- **Workspace**: WORKSPACE_BASE/users/1/langconfig-test/agents/agent_209\n\n## Workspace\n\nYour workspace directory is:\n\n    WORKSPACE_BASE/users/1/langconfig-test/agents/agent_209\n\n- **Uploaded files** — documents the user uploads (knowledge) appear in the `upload/` subfolder; read them from there when a task needs their data.\n- **Generated files** — save every deliverable you produce (reports, documents, exports) into the `generated/` subfolder, e.g. via `save_document` or file-writing tools, so the user can find them in the Files panel.\n- **Skills** — the skill catalog is staged into `skills/`; read SKILL.md files from there when a task requires a skill.\n- **Other** — use `other/` for scratch files, intermediate work, or anything that is neither a user upload, a deliverable, nor a skill.\n- **Your instructions** — AGENTS.md (this file) and CLAUDE.md sit at the workspace root.\n- Keep all files inside the workspace — do not write outside it.\n\n## Path map — use these directly, do NOT explore\n\n- User uploads: **`upload/<filename>`** (read from here)\n- Deliverables: **`generated/<filename>`** (write here)\n- Scratch / misc: **`other/<filename>`**\n- Skills: `skills/…` · Instructions: `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`\n- NEVER run ls/glob/grep just to discover paths — the brief and this map give you everything. Construct file paths from the rules above.\n\n## Working conventions\n\n- Before generating a file, match the format the user asked for (Markdown, DOCX, CSV, HTML, …) and save it with a descriptive filename inside `generated/`.\n- After producing a deliverable, summarize what you created and where it was saved.\n- If a task needs data from uploaded files, read them from `upload/` first.\n\n## Agent docs\n\n- This file (AGENTS.md) is loaded into your context as instructions on every chat run.\n- CLAUDE.md (next to this file) mirrors these instructions.\n\n\n## CLAUDE.md (embedded)\n\n# new research planner — CLAUDE.md\n\nMirror of AGENTS.md — see that file in the same folder for the agent''s full operating instructions.\n\n## Identity\n\n- **Agent ID**: 209\n- **Workspace**: WORKSPACE_BASE/users/1/langconfig-test/agents/agent_209\n\n## Quick reference\n\n- Workspace: `WORKSPACE_BASE/users/1/langconfig-test/agents/agent_209`\n- User uploads (knowledge): `upload/`; deliverables: `generated/`; scratch/misc: `other/`; skills: `skills/`.\n- After producing a deliverable, summarize what you created and where it was saved.", "include_docker": false, "use_deepagents": false, "include_chat_ui": true, "interrupt_after": null, "interrupt_before": null, "reasoning_effort": "low", "use_local_sandbox": false, "skill_router_model": null, "use_phase9_graphindex": false, "disable_memory_middleware": false, "enable_compiled_subagents": true}', '[]', '[{"name": "research-planner", "description": "Decompose a broad research topic into 4-8 focused, independent sub-queries that can be researched in parallel, covering concepts, entities, timelines, relationships and perspectives. Use when planning research, scoping a topic, breaking a question into searchable sub-questions, or before a multi-step web-research run.", "type": "dictionary", "template_id": null, "model": null, "system_prompt": "You are a research-planner specialist. Read the SKILL.md and follow its instructions exactly. Return only the result.", "tools": [], "middleware": [], "interrupt_on": {}, "skills": [], "response_format": null, "workflow_id": null, "workflow_config": null, "graph_id": null, "database": null}]', '{"type": "state", "config": {}, "mappings": null}', '{"interrupts": {}, "token_limits": {"max_total_tokens": 100000, "eviction_threshold": 80000, "summarization_threshold": 60000}, "enable_auto_eviction": true, "enable_summarization": true, "lon